# (the recipes/kimi-k3 section A configuration): the same-session control arm "A0" and the arm with the Inferact DSpark drafter "DS".
# Drafter: Inferact/Kimi-K3-DSpark @ cf6b8244620e7ea4b0651d214f28e89eac75bed6, BF16, K = 3, with --use-replayssm and the guard hook
# recipes/kimi-k3/vllm/hook/k3ds_guard.py. Run 2026-10-13 07:51-11:13 PT, one session, both GB300s, A0 first, then DS (boot 1 each; 0 retries).
# Excerpt: lines selected verbatim from the raw files named below; hostnames, IPs, user names, GPU UUIDs and private paths replaced with
# <placeholders>. Times are Pacific (PT) unless the line says otherwise; vLLM server log lines are UTC ("10-13 16:28:36" = 09:28:36 PDT).
# Definitions: decode_agg = C x 1000 / mean TPOT (tok/s, the repo's decode metric); out = output tokens / wall incl. TTFT.
# Real text = CNN/DailyMail 3.0.0 test articles (abisee/cnn_dailymail @ 96df5e68) concatenated to about 8,200 K3 prompt tokens, thinking off,
# 1,024 forced output tokens, temperature 0 (bench/kbench_chat_ds.py, pool from bench/build_pool_k3.py). Every real-text slice is disjoint from
# the other slices and replayed with a fresh per-arm nonce; "prefix_hit_pct" is the server's /metrics delta around the measured run (bar: 2).
# catid = 8,192 random-token ids in / 1,024 forced out, vllm bench serve with --temperature 0 (greedy) and 1 prompt per repetition, a fresh seed per invocation
# (kit script, NOT the repo's bench-nemotron-ultra.sh, which passes no temperature: see logs/kimi-k3/vllm-two-stations-boot-receipt.log).
# A0 is NOT bit-identical to recipes/kimi-k3 as published: it adds per-layer expert route counters (K3T_COUNT, shown in the boot line below);
# they are in both arms and cost nothing visible at C1 (A0 C1 below, 18.01, against 18.1 in the first run). The tier/pinning code of that hook was not enabled.


